{
  "title": "Aimeos Laravel \u2014 e-commerce (8,630\u2605)",
  "content": "Project: Aimeos Laravel\nDomain: e-commerce | Scale: large | Stars: 8,630\nProblem: Provides a professional, full-featured e-commerce package for Laravel that enables building ultra-fast online shops, scalable marketplaces, and complex B2B applications without starting from scratch.\nTarget users: E-commerce businesses, Marketplace operators, B2B companies, SaaS platform providers, Laravel developers\nCore features: Multi-vendor, multi-channel, multi-warehouse support; Scalable product catalog (1 to 1B+ items); JSON REST API and GraphQL administration API; Flexible payment gateway integration (100+ gateways); Subscriptions and recurring payments; Configurable product types (bundles, vouchers, subscriptions, virtual); Full-featured admin backend with dashboard; 30+ language translations with AI-based text translation\nIntegrations: 100+ payment gateways, Transifex for translations, JSON API (jsonapi.org), GraphQL\nTech stack: Vue.js + PHP/Laravel\nKey libraries: Laravel framework, Vue.js, JSON REST API, GraphQL\nArchitecture: monolith\nDesign lessons:\n- Designed as a modular, extensible Laravel package allowing seamless integration into existing applications with 5-minute setup\n- Enterprise-grade e-commerce requires configurable product systems, multi-tenancy support, and flexible pricing strategies (block/tier, customer-based)\n- API-first approach with both REST (jsonapi.org) and GraphQL enables diverse client integration and future-proofs the platform\n- Internationalization and RTL support built-in from the ground up, with 30+ language support and AI-driven translation",
